        "entry_hFtteK": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Setting Up",
            "text": "<p><strong>Assembling the Wheels</strong></p><p>1. Slide the axle into the chassis.</p><p>2. Slide the two wheels onto the chassis axle. </p><p>3. Slip the washers onto the axle and push the split pins  through the appropriate holes in the axle.</p><p>4. Clip the wheel covers onto the wheels.</p><p><strong>Assembling the Chassis to Shredder Unit</strong> </p><p>1. Rest the shredder unit on the hopper (upside down). </p><p>2. Push the wheel chassis into the 2 holes in the plastic housing of shredder. </p><p>3. Secure with the 2 screws provided.</p><p><strong>Attaching the Collection Bag</strong> </p><p>1. Stand the shredder upright and hook the collection bag into the bag mounts.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
            "collection_products_per_page": 8,
            "products": [],
            "image_loading": "",
            "video_1": "",
            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "entry_tkR4ze": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Maintenance",
            "text": "<p><strong>Reversing, Sharpening & Replacing the Blade</strong><br/></p><p>1. Remove the front part of the shredder housing. Check that the power plug is removed from the power supply.</p><p>2. Unscrew the housing interlock anticlockwise.</p><p>3. Tip forward the front part of the shredder housing. Remove it completely and put it aside.</p><p>You now have full access to the blades. </p><p>4. Use a screwdriver to block the blade plate. First, slot the screwdriver into the access hole. Then carefully turn the blade plate until one of the two blocking apertures appears and aligns with the access hole. Block the blade plate by slotting the screwdriver right<br/>through it.</p><p>5. Take out the Allen key from the recess in the housing inside the shredder. Use the Allen key to loosen the Allen bolt anticlockwise in the center of the blade plate. Remove the Allen bolt and the washer. </p><p>6. Remove the blade from its seat.</p><p>7. The blade can be reversed, otherwise sharpen or replace any blunt or damaged blade as<br/>necessary.</p><p>8. Refit the blade onto the blade plate ensuring it is seated in its correct position. </p><p>9. Refit the washer and Allen bolt and tighten securely clockwise.</p><p>10. Re-install the front part of the shredder housing onto the main housing securely. Ensure the housing interlock is tightened. </p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
